sequenceDiagram
    participant Finger
    participant TI as touch_input
    participant AI as app_input
    participant UI as chip rect<br/>(e.g. LIGHT)

    Finger->>TI: press, inside LIGHT's rect
    TI->>TI: touchPressEdge = true<br/>touchDownX/Y = contact
    AI->>UI: hitTestChips(touchDownX, touchDownY)
    UI-->>AI: PressTarget::LIGHT
    AI->>AI: capturedTarget = LIGHT
    Note over AI,UI: captured once, on the press --<br/>not re-tested again below

    Finger->>TI: finger drifts a few px<br/>while still down
    Note over Finger,TI: fingertip rolls as it leaves<br/>the glass -- normal, not an error
    TI->>TI: touchLastX/Y follows the drift
    AI->>AI: pressTarget = capturedTarget<br/>(still LIGHT: highlight tracks<br/>the capture, not the drift)

    Finger->>TI: release
    TI->>TI: touchReleaseEdge = true
    AI->>AI: chip = capturedTarget (LIGHT)
    AI->>AI: dimmerOpen = true
    Note over TI,UI: fires -- the press that captured LIGHT<br/>is what committed, drift never mattered

    rect rgb(245, 235, 235)
    Note over Finger,UI: prior behaviour (fixed 2026-08-14, commit 283b0f3):<br/>release re-ran hitTestChips() at the LIFT<br/>position instead of using the capture.<br/>A drifted lift missed the rect, so the<br/>highlight lit on press and nothing fired<br/>on release.
    end
